      },
      "message": "fix(machines): state the DNM 5700 travel as full strokes each way\n\ndoosan-dnm.mch stated Z in the machine frame (-510..0) and X/Y as half\nstrokes, so the post gate refused every move above the work origin (the\n#457 defect). It now states -1020..1020, -570..570 and -510..510, per the\ntravel rule in assets/machines/AGENTS.md.\n\nPinned in vmc_stroke.rs: the DNM bands, a plate contour passing the\nstroke check, and a 520 mm clearance still refused by name. The DNM's\noptional A has no nose_to_axis, and that separately refuses the post;\nit is filed as #1433.\n\nFixes #1410\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
