      "message": "fix(machines): split the built-in DNM 5700 into a 3-axis machine and a rotary-table variant\n\nThe DNM file declared the catalog's optional A table with no nose_to_axis,\nso the index-swing law refused every op on the built-in, even plain 3-axis\nwork at A0. No published nose-to-axis figure exists to state, and none is\ninvented: \"Doosan DNM 5700\" is now the plain 3-axis machine\n(doosan-dnm-3axis.mch), and \"Doosan DNM 5700 + rotary table\"\n(doosan-dnm.mch) keeps the A and keeps refusing by name until the setup\nstates its own nose_to_axis.\n\nFixes #1433\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
